; The warning policy is a value in the tree, not an ambient dune default (M10):
; before this stanza [dune printenv] was the only place the set existed, so a
; new module inherited whatever profile the caller ran under and a warning was
; advisory. It uses [:standard] so a future dune default still contributes,
; then pins the set this tree is clean under; [release]'s [-w -40] is
; deliberately overridden because the pinned list is the project's claim, not
; the profile's.
(env
 (_
  (flags
   (:standard -w @1..3@5..28@30..39@43@46..47@49..57@61..62@67@69-40
    -strict-sequence -strict-formats -short-paths -keep-locs))))
